Indicator 12: Financing made available for biodiversity and protected areas from sources beyond traditional external grants to governments or NGOs, and capitalisation of STP CTF endowment fund
Indicator 13: Native fast-growing charcoal-making trees planted and surviving across the forest landscape
Indicator 14: Number of improved charcoal kilns effectively in use
Indicator 15: Number of fully-dedicated professional traditional charcoal-makers harvesting unsustainably 
Indicator 16: Share of household incomes based on newly adopted sustainable livelihood activities in targeted priority communities
Indicator 17: % of female members i) in platforms and decision-making forums emplaced by the project, and ii) amongst staff recruited by and for the project
Indicator 18: % of 52 sub-indicator targets in Gender Action Plan met
Indicator 19: Quality of PIR completed a</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="FR">Considering the respective project durations and relevance of the interventions described above, the baseline investment for the project is estimated as follows: For the donor funded-projects, USD 5,862,515 for forest management and environmental law enforcement, and USD 7,217,119 for protected area management and environmental mainstreaming, for a total of USD 13,079,634. In addition, the baseline contributions by the three lead government agencies relevant to the project, DGA, DFB and RSESD, amount to an estimated USD 516,000, USD 306,000 and USD 282,000 over the duration of the project. The total project baseline scenario therefore is estimated to USD 14,183,634</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="FR">- Hiring of rest of core project team - Gender specialist, Principe Technical liaison, Communication/M&amp;E specialist
- Strenghtening of institutional framework on biodiversity, targeting Principe
- Develop and validate updated management plans for national parks in Principe and Sao Tome
- Develop sustainable finance plan for biodiversity
- Support alternatives to wood based charcoal
- Launch a sustainable charcoal platform
- Develop and validate a communication strategy for the project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="FR">- M&amp;E/communication specialist hired in April, Principe technical liaison hired in June, lead Gender specialist hired in September
- Periodic review of the UNESCO Biosphere developed, validated and presented by the President of the Principe Government
- 2021-2025 management plan of the Sao Tome National Park developed, validated and officially presented by Authorities
- Capacity building needs and gaps of national counterparts identified in a participatory exercise
- Sustainable finance strategy for biodiversity developed and validated
- Consultancy hired to develop a Conservation Trust Fund
- Backstopping provided to the launch and commercialization of the first nationally produced sustainable charcoal, made of coconut briquettes
- Sustainable charcoal platform launched in July 
- project communication strategy developed and validated</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
